# Line-ending policy.
#
# Everything is stored LF in the repository AND checked out LF in the working
# tree. This project is edited from Windows but runs inside Linux containers
# (the backend bind-mounts the repo at /app), so a CRLF checkout means the
# container reads CRLF files. `eol=lf` keeps a Windows checkout, a WSL
# checkout and the container byte-identical, and stops Git printing
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF" on every commit.
#
# `text=auto` still lets Git detect binary content and leave it untouched;
# the explicit rules below are belt-and-braces for files where a wrong guess
# would corrupt them.
* text=auto eol=lf

# --- binary: never convert -------------------------------------------------
*.ico  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf  binary
*.mp4  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary

# --- must stay LF ----------------------------------------------------------
# ClamAV parses signature files line by line and a trailing CR becomes part of
# the pattern, so a CRLF checkout silently breaks malware detection.
*.ndb text eol=lf
# Read by clamd inside the container.
*.conf text eol=lf
*.sh   text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf

# --- must stay CRLF --------------------------------------------------------
# cmd.exe mis-parses LF-only batch files.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# --- diff hygiene ----------------------------------------------------------
# Lockfiles are generated; keep them out of review diffs.
package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated
